# Packages cleanup-ubuntu.sh never removes. One name per line, "*" matches
# anything. Add your company's agents here, or in
# ~/.config/dotfiles/cleanup.d/protect-packages.list (kept outside the repo).
#
# Packages installed from a repository outside Ubuntu's archive, and local
# .debs, are kept automatically as well (that is how corporate agents look);
# the dry run lists them. The drop list below wins over both.

# system: kernels, drivers, firmware, OEM, desktop base
linux-*
nvidia-*
libnvidia-*
realtek-*
firmware-*
oem-*
ubuntu-*
opensc
libnss-resolve
systemd-coredump

# corporate agents
falcon-sensor
icaclient
intune-portal
microsoft-*
packages-microsoft-prod
ud-agent
zscaler*
cisco*
